---
name: cycle-anchor-drift-monitor
description: Multi-month KPI cycle anchor invariants — per-cycle-window uniqueness, oldest-row-wins repair, and prevention trigger (ADR-091, supersedes ADR-090)
type: constraint
---
`kpis.frequency_cycle_start` is a PER-CYCLE-WINDOW invariant (ADR-091):
two rows in the same `(employee_id, kpi_name, review_year, frequency)` tuple
whose `review_period` falls inside the SAME canonical cycle window MUST
share the same anchor. Different cycle windows in the same year (e.g.
Quarterly Apr-Jun coexisting with Jul-Sep) are explicitly allowed —
`frequency_cycle_start` is a per-row window label, not a yearly series tag.
Enforced by trigger `trg_enforce_intra_year_cycle_anchor_consistency`
(BEFORE INSERT). UPDATEs are intentionally exempt so the repair RPC and admin
propagation paths can converge anchors.

**Repair contract.** When divergence is found within the same canonical
cycle window, call
use `public.repair_intra_year_cycle_anchor_drift(p_dry_run, p_safety_ceiling)`.
Strategy: oldest-row-wins **per canonical window** (smallest `created_at`,
ties by id ASC). Only
`frequency_cycle_start` is mutated. Every change writes
`kpi_audit_logs.action='KPI_CYCLE_ANCHOR_REPAIRED'` with
`metadata.policy='ADR-091'`,
`metadata.strategy='oldest_row_wins_per_window'`,
`metadata.cycle_window=<window>`. Safety
ceiling defaults to 500 rows. Repair is reversible from the audit log.

**Detector.** `public.detect_intra_year_cycle_anchor_drift()` returns one row
per drifted `(employee, kpi_name, year, frequency, cycle_window)` tuple
(anchors[] + affected_row_count). Cheap GROUP BY HAVING; safe to call from
a daily monitor. **Schema change (ADR-091):** the result set now carries a
`cycle_window` column; the function was dropped and re-created.

**Pure-helper SSOT.**
- `src/lib/cycleAnchorRepair.ts::planAnchorRepairs` — repair selection.
- `src/lib/cycleAnchorWindowConsistency.ts::checkCycleAnchorConflict` —
  mirrors the trigger predicate (ADR-091). Regression locked by
  `src/test/cycleAnchorWindowConsistency.test.ts` (V.A.V.S.S. Ganapathi
  Varma May→June cross-cycle scenario + Sajid same-window drift).

**Anti-pattern.** Do NOT call `public.resolve_cycle_anchor(frequency, month_idx)`
(2-arg) on rows that already have an anchor — it returns Jan-anchored
windows and overwrites legitimate offset cycles. Always use the 3-arg
sticky overload `(frequency, month_idx, existing_anchor)` per ADR-088.

